-- title:
--   Base change to ℚ̄ respects restriction of places
-- statement:
--   Let $F_0,F_0'$ be intermediate fields of $\mathbf{Q}$ in $\mathbf{Q}((q))$, let $\varphi_0\colon F_0\to F_0'$ be an integral ring homomorphism, and let $\bar\varphi$ be an integral $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-algebra map between the fields `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F₀` and `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F₀'` (the $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-subfields of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of $F_0$, $F_0'$), compatible with $\varphi_0$ in the sense that $\bar\varphi(1\otimes f)=1\otimes\varphi_0 f$ under the isomorphisms `baseChangeEquiv` of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}\otimes_{\mathbf{Q}}F_0$, $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}\otimes_{\mathbf{Q}}F_0'$ with these fields. Let $M_0,M_0'$ be curve models over $\mathbf{Q}$ of $F_0,F_0'$ (integral schemes, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Q}$, with an identification of the field with the function field over the base and a bijection from closed points to places whose valuation rings are the images of the stalks), and let $\pi_0\colon M_0'\to M_0$ be a morphism over $\mathbf{Q}$ which is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation and which on generic stalks is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\varphi_0$ read through the two function-field identifications. Let $M_\eta,M_\eta'$ be curve models over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of the two base-changed fields, equipped with isomorphisms $e_\eta,e_{\eta'}$ onto the pullbacks $M_0\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Q}}\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, $M_0'\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Q}}\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, such that for every $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-section $x$ of $M_\eta$ (resp. $y$ of $M_{\eta'}$) lying over a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0$ (resp. $y_0$ of $M_0'$) via the first projection, the preimage of the valuation ring of the place `pointEquivPlace` of $x$ (resp. $y$) along $F_0\to\overline{\mathbf{Q}}\otimes_{\mathbf{Q}}F_0\cong$ `laurentBaseChange …` is the valuation ring of the place of $x_0$ (resp. $y_0$). Then for $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-sections $y$ of $M_{\eta'}$ and $x$ of $M_\eta$ whose images agree under the pullback of $\pi_0$, i.e. $y$ followed by $e_{\eta'}$ and by the map of pullbacks induced by $(\pi_0,\mathrm{id},\mathrm{id})$ equals $x$ followed by $e_\eta$, the place attached to $x$ equals the restriction along $\bar\varphi$ of the place attached to $y$, that is, its valuation subring is the preimage under $\bar\varphi$ of the valuation subring of the place of $y$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of base change to $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with restriction of places: a finite flat morphism of smooth proper curves over $\mathbf{Q}$, read on $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-models of the base-changed function fields, carries $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-points to $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-points in the way the function-field embedding dictates. It is the input that allows the geometric description of the Hecke correspondence by two finite morphisms defined over $\mathbf{Q}$ to be compared, on $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-points, with the definition of Hecke operators by pull-back and norm of places; it is used in the construction of Hecke endomorphisms of relative Jacobians attached to rational curve models.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_pointEquivPlace_comp_eq_restrictAlong_of_baseChange.lean

